 north-west. Set on Bloomsbury's grid at about 30° (Great Russell Street's angle in the OpenStreetMap ground, which lacked the museum's own footprint). From general knowledge of the plan (the court is about 92 by 73 m); no photographs were available. Column counts, wing depths and the northern buildings are approximate."}